{
  "_comment": "EVERY CLAUSE THE FLOW HAS DECLARED, by identity and not by count. `liar_census.clause_floor_shortfall` compares this against `flow/phase1_phase2_phase3.yaml` and `test_liar_census::test_nothing_the_flow_declares_is_left_unswept` blocks on the result.",
  "_what_fails": "MISSING -- an entry here that the flow no longer declares. That is the silent shrink this record exists to catch, and the failure names the clause rather than a number.",
  "_what_does_not_fail": "SURPLUS -- a clause the flow declares that is not yet recorded. A GROW never reopens the test. That is deliberate and it is the whole reason this file replaced a literal: the number it replaced went stale SEVEN times, every one of them a grow, because the flow's own author had to remember a count living in a test file.",
  "_how_to_authorise_a_shrink": "Delete the entry BY HAND, in the same change that removes the clause from the flow, and say why in that commit. `liar_census.record_clause_floor` REFUSES to do it for you: it only ever adds, because dropping an entry is exactly how a shrink would be authorised by accident.",
  "_how_to_refresh_after_a_grow": "python3 -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'tools'); import liar_census as lc; lc.record_clause_floor()\"  -- additive only, safe to run without judgement, and it refuses if anything is MISSING.",
